New zyppci
==========


As root@zyppci
--------------

=== Login as root and add your ssh key to ~.ssh/authorized_keys

=== (adjust timezone: timedatectl set-timezone Europe/Berlin)

=== echo <<EOF >/etc/motd.d/zci
   ____ _   __ __ ___     ___ _
  |__  / \ / / . \ . \   /  _| |
    / / \ V /|  _/  _/   | / | |
   / /__ | | | | | |     | \_| |
  /_____||_| |_| |_|     \___|_| is hosted here!
                                 Please don't mess it up ;)
  Contact: #discuss-zypp, ma, bzeller


EOF

=== If with legacy docker containers:
zypper in docker docker-compose
systemctl enable docker
systemctl start docker

=== User zci: uid=1000(zci) gid=1000(zci) groups=1000(zci),469(docker)
    (docker.zci/env must match uid/gid)
groupadd -g 1000 zci
useradd -u 1000 -g zci -G docker zci
echo <<EOF >/etc/sudoers.d/zci
%zci ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
EOF

=== Add your ssh key to ~zci/.ssh/authorized_keys
su - zci
mkdir .ssh
chmod 700 .ssh
vi .ssh/authorized_keys
exit

- Install other needed packages:
git gitk git-gui git-lfs podman cron
osc build obs-service-go_modules obs-service-obs_scm obs-service-obs_scm-common obs-service-tar_scm obs-service-recompress obs-service-set_version

#systemctl enable cron
#systemctl start cron


As zci@zyppci
--------------
[see bashrc]
##################################################
export ZCI_USER_CONFIGDIR=~/.config/zypp-team
export ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT=~/zypp-ci-utils
export ZCI_WORKSPACE=~/ZCI_WORKSPACE
if [ -d "$ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT" ]; then
    PATH="$ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT/zypp-team/bin:$PATH"
fi
[ -z "$SSH_AUTH_SOCK" -a -f . ~/.ssh4cron ] && . ~/.ssh4cron
##################################################

Setup:

- Copy the zypp-team-submittkey to ~/.ssh
- Launch an ssh-agent
Call ($ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT/zypp-team/bin/)ssh4cron to launch an ssh-agent
if not yet running and add the zypp-team-submittkey (passphrase needed). You
can call it anytime to make sure the key is available (e.g. after reboot).

(The launched agents env vars are stored in ~/.ssh4cron. Sourcing it gives you
access to the agent. That's done by bashrc if ~/.ssh4cron

- Get the zypp-ci-utils project:
# cd ~
# git config --global user.name 'zypp ci'
# git config --global user.email zypp-internal@suse.com
# git config --global pull.rebase true
# git clone git@github.com:openSUSE/zypp-ci-utils.git


- Copy and setups config files: In $ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT"/zypp-team/cfg:
# cp bashrc ~/.bashrc
# cp bash_profile ~/.bash_profile
# (exec bash)

# mkdir --parents "$ZCI_USER_CONFIGDIR"
# cp gitea-config  oscrc "$ZCI_USER_CONFIGDIR"
Set auth tokens in oscrc and gitea-config so the configuration allows to
access IBS/OBS/GITEA as user zypp-team. Extending the PATH will then provide
git-ibs-zt  git-obs-zt  isc-zt  osc-zt commands to access IBS/OBS/GITEA as user
zypp-team. Scripts in "$ZCI_UTILS_CHECKOUT/zypp-team/bin" will refer to these
commands.

# cp Cron* ~/bin
Setup for cron (crontab -e) (later, if everyting is done)



---
# ###########################################################################
MAILTO="zypp-maintainers@suse.de"
# ###########################################################################
# m h   D M WD (0 or 7 is Sun)
42 */1  * * *   $HOME/bin/CronChecks
13 5    * * *   $HOME/bin/CronDaily
13 6    * * 1   $HOME/bin/CronWeekly
# ###########################################################################
*/10 *  * * *   $HOME/zypp-ci-utils/zypp-team/bin/ZCI --silent
---

- Setup the ZCI_WORKSPACE:
# mkdir --parents "$ZCI_WORKSPACE"
# touch "$ZCI_WORKSPACE"/.giteastats

The magic .giteastats file is needed to enable using this directory for all
kinds of necessary checkouts.

##################################################
ZCI (ATM via docker):

- Workspace for the docker based ZCI container defined in zypp-ci-utils/docker.zci.
# mkdir --parents ~/DOCKER_ZCI_WORKSPACE
See also the zypp-ci-utils/docker.zci/README and "ZCI --help" (OUTSIDE THE CONTAINER!)
Triggered by cron (crontab -l).

